rface":"elevated"},"id":"tooltip-card","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"viewHeader.lockedHint"},"tone":"highlighted","variant":"label"},"id":"tooltip-text","type":"Text"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"align":"start","direction":"horizontal","padding":"0 0 0 120px","visible":false},"id":"tooltip-rename","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"card":true,"padding":"4px 8px","radius":6,"surface":"elevated"},"id":"tooltip-rename-card","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"viewHeader.edit"},"tone":"highlighted","variant":"label"},"id":"tooltip-rename-text","type":"Text"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"direction":"vertical","gap":8,"padding":"12px 12px 0","visible":false},"id":"toast-tray","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"icon":"circle-check","title":{"$i18n":"viewHeader.saved"},"toast":true,"tone":"success","visible":false},"id":"toast-saved","type":"Alert"},{"config":{"icon":"circle-alert","title":{"$i18n":"viewHeader.saveFailed"},"toast":true,"tone":"danger","visible":false},"id":"toast-failed","type":"Alert"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"frameFollowsTheme":true,"frameMinHeight":"420px","frameWidth":"880px","label":{"$i18n":"canvas.label"}},"id":"canvas","slots":{"frame":[{"config":{"direction":"vertical","gap":12,"padding":24},"id":"mock","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"mock.payment.title"},"variant":"title"},"id":"mock-title","type":"Text"},{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"mock.payment.submit"},"variant":"primary"},"id":"mock-submit","type":"Button"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"CanvasStage"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"RootShell"},"name":"View page: header","spec":{"accessibility":["The header is a landmark-free strip; the name is the level-1 heading and, while editing, stays as a hidden heading. The rename button is named \"Rename Checkout or change its feature tag\" and, while locked, stays focusable with its reason as its description.","The form fields have visible labels; the error is tied to its field; the alerts are announced; touch tiers give the rename and delete buttons 44px targets."],"constraints":["Built only from Adapter Widgets (Stack, Text, Badge, Button, TextInput, Alert, CanvasStage); no Widget outside the Adapter catalog. The canvas below the header is the mock View of the Workbench View and is not part of the header.","The form replaces the row and a Variant shows one of them, because a Widget cannot swap its own content; the disabled rename button, the Save in progress and the disabled Save are second Widgets swapped in by a Variant. The tooltip of the disabled rename is a card under the header, because the Adapter has no Tooltip.","The strings of the app are copied under the same Locale keys; parameters are the Widget values. The View name and tag are sample content, and the reasons of an invalid save are the server's own text (viewHeader.sample.invalid); the lock badge is one baked sample sentence (viewHeader.sample.lockBadge) because a Badge takes one parameter.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A member opened a View (/views/<id>); the header sits above the render-context bar and the canvas and is on every device tier. The sidebar, navbar and canvas are in the Workbench View.","The base state is a member who may write Views: the name, the feature tag, the rename button and the delete action (offered on a desktop window only). Variants show the form, its errors and its save, the lease another member holds, the conflict, and what a member who cannot write sees.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; the Workbench chrome follows the Workbench language, so its text is baked here per Locale. The View name, its feature tag, the lease holder and the times are sample content."],"intent":"Show the header of a View page as built from Adapter Widgets only: the View's name as the page heading, its feature tag and the edit lease, with the in-place rename and feature edit, the edit lease and the revision conflict a save can meet.","interactionRules":["The name is the page's level-1 heading and the feature tag a quiet badge beside it, read as \"Feature checkout\" by assistive technology; a View without a tag shows none. A member with the write key renames the View and sets or clears its tag in place on every tier, tablet and phone included; renaming is not structural editing.","Rename opens a form with the name and the feature tag; Save is the primary action, Cancel keeps nothing and Escape cancels. An empty name is refused beside the field; an empty tag clears the tag, as the field's help says; a save the server refuses as invalid lists its reasons and keeps the form.","While someone else holds the View's edit lease the rename button is disabled and says why, the form cannot be opened or saved, and the header shows who holds it until when; a member with the force-release key gets Release lock. A save refused because a lease was taken meanwhile says who holds it until when and that the draft is kept.","A save made on an older revision is never overwritten: the form stays with the draft, the header says the View changed and shows what it is now (name and tag), and the member chooses Keep editing mine, which bases the next save on the new revision, or Discard mine.","A saved change says so in a notice and re-reads the View; a save that failed for another reason says so in a notice. Deleting the View is structural: the delete action opens on a desktop window for a member with the write key, after the impact is shown (Delete: View and UX Flow dialogs)."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"},{"relation":"delete-dialogs","type":"view","viewId":"c5f2a106-7b3e-4d19-8a26-3e9d1c0b5f06"},{"relation":"page","type":"view","viewId":"7f3